 "about": "One run of the soft-promise check: its answers to each case. Each case's expected, code_blocked and outcome are as of the run, from the case file and the code check as they were then. `python -m evals.calibration.soft_promise --rescore <this file>` scores the answers against the case file as it is now and is the authority; a case whose input_sha256 (of its arm's language, prose, cards and, in the new shape, next_steps) the case file no longer matches is stale there, and its answers aren't scored.",
